  "resolutions": {
    "LOCATION_CATALOG_SCHEMA": "The canonical V2 catalog contains exactly two records in V1 order: start_path then dark_forest. Required immutable fields are location_id, localized name, description, level_min, level_max, unlock_level, boss name and mob-name references. Unknown IDs fail closed; no fabricated fallback record is created.",
    "LOCALIZED_NAME_AND_TECHNICAL_ID_POLICY": "Technical IDs remain start_path and dark_forest. User-visible resolvers return 🌿 Початок Шляху and 🌲 Темний Бір. Technical IDs must never be title-cased or exposed as fallback presentation; unknown IDs use an explicit unavailable result.",
    "UNLOCK_AND_LEVEL_POLICY": "Початок Шляху covers levels 1-5 and unlocks at level 1. Темний Бір covers levels 6-10 and unlocks at level 6. Unlock enumeration preserves catalog order and does not skip the level gate.",
    "GRAPH_TRAVEL_AND_RESTART_POLICY": "The world graph contains city, start_path and dark_forest. Edges are city<->start_path<->dark_forest, symmetric and duplicate-free. Catalog and graph are static declarative content, so restart rebuilds the same values without migration or runtime mutation.",
    "MOB_NPC_QUEST_REFERENCE_POLICY": "Location references use only stable technical IDs and must resolve against the two-location catalog. Mob lists and the two boss names are copied from V1 catalog evidence. NPC and quest catalogs remain separate owners and must pass referential validation; this parity stage invents no NPC, quest, mob or location.",
    "CONSUMER_ALLOWLIST_AND_SHADOW_CATALOGS": "Allowed consumers are world/travel, map presentation, hunting/mob selection, story navigation, quest/NPC validation and test fixtures. The V2 catalog is the single definition owner. Presentation aliases, graph nodes and content references are consumers, not parallel editable catalogs."
  },
